  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sasidharan Pillai vs Thekkumbhagham Grama Panchayath on 29 August, 2016 Author: K.Vinod Chandran Bench: K.Vinod Chandran In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr.Justice K.Vinod Chandran Monday, The 29Th Dayof August 2016/7Th Bhadra, 1938 WP(C).No. 819 of 2010 (B) -------------------------- Petitioner(S): ----------------------- Sasidharan Pillai, S/O. Sukumara Pillai, Thamaralsasi Mandiram, 2, Thekkumbhagom. P.O, Kollam. By Adv. Sri.P.Chandrasekhar. Respondent(S): -------------------------- 1. Thekkumbhagham Grama Panchayath, Represented By Its Secretary, Chavara South, Pin - 691 584. 2. The Secretary, Thekkumbhagham Grama Panchayath, Represented By Its Secretary, Chavara South, Pin - 691 584. 3. P.Natarajan, Kailas Bhavan, Maranad. P.O,Ezhukon, Kollam. R1 & R2 By Adv. Sri.K.Subash Chandra Bose. R3 By Advs. Sri.D.Ajithkumar, Smt.Laliza.T.Y., Sasidharan Pillai vs Thekkumbhagham Grama Panchayath on 29 August, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/21540257/",
    "facts": "The prayer in the writ petition is to direct respondents 1 and 2, the Panchayat, to prohibit establishment of a Cashew factory and its operation using electric power without obtaining consent under Section 233 of the Kerala Panchayat Raj Act, 1994 ('Act of 1994' for short) and the consent of the Kerala State Pollution Control Board.",
    "arguments": "3. The learned Counsel appearing for the 3rd respondent submits that both the consent under Section 233 of the Act of 1994 and consent of the Pollution Control Board has been obtained and the 3rd respondent has been carrying on the Cashew factory for some time and then disposed it of.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. The learned Counsel appearing for the 3rd respondent submits that both the consent under Section 233 of the Act of 1994 and consent of the Pollution Control Board has been obtained and the 3rd respondent has been carrying on the Cashew factory for some time and then disposed it of.",
